  "description": "This course will prepare the students with tools to evaluate mineral resources and mining projects from industrial perspectives. Students are expected to possess basic understanding of geostatistics, economic and accounting principles, and the mining industry in general. This course will provide additional insight in geostatistical methods and the economic and financial decision-making process. Case studies will examine recent major global exploration undertakings to reinforce key concepts.",
